  "body": "Currently, the way to have Canvas2D-generated content in WebGL involves:\r\n\r\n```\r\ngl.bindTexture(gl.TEXTURE_2D, texture);\r\ngl.texImage2D(gl.TEXTURE_2D, 0, gl.RGBA, gl.RGBA, gl.UNSIGNED_BYTE, canvas)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis needs to be executed every time there's a change on the `canvas`, which may be annoying since there's no easy way to detect a `canvas` is dirty. More problematic, this necessarily involves a copy of data from the canvas object to the WebGL texture.\r\n\r\nUsing `OffscreenCanvas` we should be able to provide a way to attach an OffscreenCanvas to a WebGL texture, meaning a 2D context can be created that directly renders to the WebGL texture, avoiding any copies.",
  "closed_by": null,
